<title>NORWAY: SAS to expand joint flights with Lufthansa.</title>
<headline>SAS to expand joint flights with Lufthansa.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scandinavian Airlines System (SAS) and German carrier Lufthansa, will introduce jointly coded flights to eight more international destinations, Oslo Bourse said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The measure will take effect on December 1, the statement said.</p>
<p>The two airlines will thus cover more than 2,000 jointly coded flights per week to 51 cities, both overseas and in Europe. it said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
